<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">arrest</ansi>

When you commit crimes in a town, the local guards will eventually
come for you. What happens then depends on your <ansi fg="command">arrest policy</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Surrender</ansi> (the default): you go quietly. A guard hauls you off to
a holding cell to serve a sentence. You can wait it out, or pay a
<ansi fg="command">fine</ansi> to leave early (see <ansi fg="command">help fine</ansi>). Either way, serving your
time clears your record with that faction.

<ansi fg="yellow">Resist</ansi>: you refuse to be taken. The guards drop the pretense and
fight you for real. Guards are trained and well-equipped, and they
back each other up -- resisting is dangerous.

After a guard announces an arrest you have a few moments to decide:
draw a weapon and you have chosen to resist; do nothing and you are
taken in.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">set arrest</ansi>
    Show your current arrest policy.

  <ansi fg="command">set arrest surrender</ansi>
    Go quietly when arrested (default).

  <ansi fg="command">set arrest resist</ansi>
    Fight the guards rather than be taken.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">justice</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">fine</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">payfine</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">bounty</ansi>
